# dependencies
node_modules/

# secrets — .env holds AI provider keys; only .env.example is tracked
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
secrets.env

# the Vercel CLI's link to the project — which account and which project this directory deploys to,
# written by `vercel link`. Not a secret, but it is per-developer: a second person cloning this repo
# links their own, and `vercel env pull` drops real environment values into .env.local, which the
# lines above already keep out. Vercel gitignores it by default and so do we.
.vercel

# logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# editor / tool state
# Impeccable keeps three different things in here and they do not belong on the same side of this
# line. config.json is the SHARED design-detector config — which rules are ignored for this project
# and why — so it is a project decision and belongs in the repo. config.local.json is explicitly
# per-developer, and hook.cache.json is per-session scratch. Ignoring the whole directory meant a
# "shared" ignore was never shared: it would not survive a fresh clone or a second machine.
# `**/` because there is more than one of these: the detector writes beside whichever directory the
# CLI was run from, so there is one at the repo root and one under app/. A root-anchored pattern
# covered only the first, and the second was being held back by .git/info/exclude — which is local
# to one clone and would not protect anybody else.
# The two were since merged into the root one (paths relative to the repo root): run Impeccable
# from the repo root so a second app/.impeccable/ does not grow back.
**/.impeccable/*
!**/.impeccable/config.json
# Surface briefs hold each screen's direction contract, which later sessions reload before editing
# that screen, so they are project decisions like config.json, not scratch.
!**/.impeccable/surfaces/
# design.json is DESIGN.md's machine-readable sidecar (tokens, component snippets) — the design
# system, not scratch.
!**/.impeccable/design.json

# per-student saves, when the file backend is in use (`npm start` on a laptop). Hosted, these live
# in a KV store instead — see app/store.js. This is somebody's actual work, not build output, so it
# is ignored rather than cleaned.
app/.data/

# build-time scratch for the Phaser reference: the downloaded source tarball at the pinned tag, the
# extracted tree, and the 28 MB doclet dump jsdoc produces from it. All of it is regenerable with
# `npm run build:docs`, and what actually gets committed is app/public/phaser-docs, which is built
# from it. See app/tools/build-phaser-doclets.js.
app/.cache/

# captured tester sessions — what children asked the assistant, word for word, plus every error
# their game threw. Written by `npm run session:watch`, read by `npm run session:report`. It stays
# on the laptop that captured it: this is minors' free text and it has no business in a repository.
app/logs/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# scratch
*.bak

# Impeccable skill (.claude/skills/impeccable, installed with `npx impeccable install
# --providers=claude --scope=project`). The skill text is committed so every session — cloud ones
# included — has /impeccable. Two things it writes are not: the 16MB engine binary, which is
# per-platform and which the launcher re-downloads (pinned, from GitHub) into ~/.impeccable/bin on
# first use; and settings.local.json, where the installer puts its edit/Stop detector hook. That file
# is per-machine by Claude Code's own convention — moving the hook into settings.json would run the
# detector in every session for everyone, which is a separate decision.
.claude/skills/impeccable/scripts/bin/
.claude/settings.local.json
